#Siemens MF-Tyre/MF-Swift setting data
DELFT_TYRE_SW 30125
DELFT_TYRE_TVM 0
#MiscYellow0
*CPAR_INCLUDE  Extensions\MFTyre_MFSwift
*CPAR_INCLUDE  Extensions\TNO_DelftTyre
#ENDMYellow

DELFT_TYRE_INIT

*DELFT_TYRE_DATA Extensions\MFTyre_MFSwift\Siemens_car205_60R15_TV.tir

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This tire data selects the model option "Siemens MF-Tyre/MF-Swift", which adopts MF-Tyre/MF-Swift model and bypass the CarSim internal tire model.  In this option, MF-Tyre/MF-Swift calculates all tire forces and moments, and also searches a tire/ground contact point or an effective contact plane.
#
#Users are allowed to select several types of options in each of categories: Tire side, Contact method, Dynamics and Slip forces.
#
#In this dataset, the Dynamics is chosen as "Transient (< 10Hz, non-linear)" and Slip forces is chosen as "+Turnslip." This option will be able to calculate tire dynamics up to 10 Hz with turn-slip steering torque especially under a low speed parking maneuver.
#
#RT Libraryies are also specified that the dataset can be used for real-time simulation with DS1006 system and QNX/LNX base system.
#
#MF-Swift license is required in order to execute the simulation in off-line and on-line real-time simulation.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Tire (External); { MF-Tyre/MF-Swift } 205/60 R15 (Swift, Turn-Slip)
#Library : Tire (External)
#DataSet : 205/60 R15 (Swift, Turn-Slip)
